WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.402
I want to start with a field on

2
00:00:01.402 --> 00:00:01.690
a form.

3
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:02.780
Cultural needs.

4
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.794
And the answer, again and again, is none

5
00:00:05.794 --> 00:00:06.110
identified.

6
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.900
Honestly, that question feels awkward to ask.

7
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.490
People usually mention what matters to them.

8
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.615
Usually they don't, at least not to someone

9
00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:16.580
from an agency.

10
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.190
And Minnesota law treats it as part of

11
00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:19.710
the process.

12
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.229
For people using waiver services, informed decision making

13
00:00:23.229 --> 00:00:26.317
includes identification of the person's cultural needs and

14
00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:29.020
access to culturally responsive services and providers.

15
00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.754
So how do you ask without it being

16
00:00:31.754 --> 00:00:32.490
awkward or stereotyping?

17
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.820
Open questions about what matters.

18
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.015
What's important to you in how people help

19
00:00:37.015 --> 00:00:37.670
you at home?

20
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.556
Anything about your faith, food or routines helpers

21
00:00:40.556 --> 00:00:41.200
should know?

22
00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.250
Who do you want with you when decisions

23
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:43.690
are made?

24
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.820
Which language are you most comfortable in?

25
00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.663
And not, people from that community usually prefer

26
00:00:49.663 --> 00:00:50.070
this.

27
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.300
Exactly.

28
00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:53.550
Background can suggest a question.

29
00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.200
It never answers it.

30
00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.930
Say the person wants helpers who speak their

31
00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.090
language, and there aren't any in the county.

32
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:01.520
Widen the search.

33
00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:04.910
Ask navigators and community organizations what they know.

34
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.551
Ask providers specific questions about what they could

35
00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:07.840
adapt.

36
00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.110
Bring the options back and let the person

37
00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:10.350
choose.

38
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.060
And record honestly what you looked for and

39
00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:13.640
didn't find.

40
00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.570
Why record the gap?

41
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.180
Because a hidden gap never gets fixed.

42
00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:20.270
One record is a person's story.

43
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.408
A pattern of the same gap is something

44
00:01:22.408 --> 00:01:23.500
the program can act on.

45
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.550
And in the plan itself?

46
00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.240
Be specific, in the person's words.

47
00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:31.130
Prefers family tells a new helper almost nothing.

48
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.827
Wants their sister present for decisions, prefers a

49
00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:36.114
female helper for bathing, tells them what to

50
00:01:36.114 --> 00:01:36.400
do.

51
00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.390
And ask again when life changes.
